// #############################################################################
//  Virtual Interface - mirrors the DUT's I/O pins.
//
//  All fields are non-const references into the Verilated DUT struct so both
//  the driver (writes inputs) and monitors (read outputs) share the same view.
//
//  The Driver base receives a `const VIF*` - use const_cast in drive() when
//  you need to write to input fields (this is intentional: only the driver
//  mutates inputs, verified by convention not by the type system).
//
//  TODO: add / remove fields to match {{DUT_CLASS}}'s port list.
// #############################################################################

